  "notes": [
    "Token ids and names come from the AtlasLoot parse (vendor/atlasloot/data-tbc.lua row comments); zone and boss from data/atlasloot_sources.json keyed on the TOKEN id. The TBC tier tokens do not appear in db.json at all, so no classAllowlist or tooltip witnesses their class grouping.",
    "Set piece ids come from db.json by `setId`, and the piece-to-token pairing is a SLOT JOIN on db.json's `type` field, not a witnessed redemption list. No committed input states which token buys which piece. The join reproduces both committed files (ret 18 entries, feral 15) exactly, which is a consistency check rather than an independent one.",
    "T4/T5 group: Champion. T6 group: Protector. The T6 vocabulary is Conqueror/Vanquisher/Protector and the class triples are RE-CUT, not renamed -- paladin goes Champion->Conqueror but druid goes Defender->Vanquisher. See data/two-hop/feral-tokens.json notes 9-10, which record that 'druid uses the Defender-equivalent' would have been wrong.",
    "SME GATE ITEM: the T6 triples are witnessed in-repo by feral-tokens.json (Vanquisher = Rogue/Mage/Druid, Protector = Warrior/Hunter/Shaman, leaving Conqueror = Paladin/Priest/Warlock). The T4/T5 HERO column (hunter/mage/warlock) is NOT witnessed by any committed file -- it is elimination against paladin=Champion and druid=Defender, the only two anchors. Confirm before trust."
  ],
